<article class="env-lemma" id="08AE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08AE">Lemma <span data-tag="08AE">33.35.16</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $n \geq 0$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent sheaf on $\mathbf{P}^ n_ k$ with Hilbert polynomial $P \in \mathbf{Q}[t]$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  P(d) = \dim _ k H^0(\mathbf{P}^ n_ k, \mathcal{F}(d))  \]
</div>
  <p> for all $d \gg 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the vanishing of cohomology of high enough twists of $\mathcal{F}$. See Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01YS" data-tag="01YS">30.14.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>